Reproducible probe: `workflow/due-dilligence-performance/remediation/wp8_probe.py`

Both commands ran from the `performance-analysis` framework worktree in
separate fresh processes. The probe creates and removes one temporary BREP;
it does not modify a project or historical audit asset. It uses a tiny local
counter wrapper rather than `Mock`, deletes each returned placed shape, and
runs `gc.collect()` before every RSS sample. The nearly-flat RSS samples below
are therefore post-forced-collection observations, not evidence of ordinary
runtime RSS behavior.

Bounded command:

    PYTHONPATH="$PWD" /home/asa/devel/libresolid-studio/.venv/bin/python workflow/due-dilligence-performance/remediation/wp8_probe.py --mode bounded --counts 1000 4000 8000

